{%- comment -%}
  Paste this into the TRMNL Private Plugin "Markup" editor for the
  weather-yr plugin (Polling strategy). Field names match the JSON
  produced by fetch.mjs (see data.json / README.md in this folder).

  This is view-only markup: do NOT include <div class="screen">/"view">
  wrappers - TRMNL's platform provides those automatically for private
  plugins. Only Layout + Title Bar.

  Font note: TRMNL renders pixel fonts by default on low-density e-ink
  devices. Forcing smooth Inter instead normally requires a device-wide
  "Text Scale" setting (screen--text-scale-*, applied to the outer
  .screen element, which private plugins don't control). Instead we set
  font-family directly here, scoped to just this plugin, which overrides
  the pixel font without touching device-wide settings or other plugins.

  Top section: weather icon, BIG (144px, up from the old 96px hero-row
  size) and alone/centered above the temperature and condition text -
  previously the icon sat in a 3-column hero row next to the temperature
  and clothing icons; now it's its own centered block at the very top so
  it reads as the headline element, with the temperature/condition text
  stacked directly underneath it (still centered).

  Bottom section: the clothing proposal icon(s) (current.clothing_icon_url,
  plus current.rain_gear_icon_url / current.wind_gear_icon_url when
  applicable) moved OUT of the hero row and down to their own centered row
  at the very bottom of the card, together with the clothing/rain text
  that explains them - previously these sat squeezed next to the weather
  icon and temperature in the same hero row.

  All icon <img> tags use class="image image--contain image-dither" - NOT
  just "image". broforce's portrait images (plugins/broforce/template*.liquid)
  are the one confirmed-working example of a custom-generated icon on this
  same TRMNL account, and they use exactly these two extra classes;
  weather-yr's icons only had the bare "image" class and were rendering as
  a generic placeholder glyph in every view regardless of icon file, size,
  or PNG bit-depth. image-dither is described by TRMNL's own framework docs
  as "essential" for images on 1-bit e-ink displays. That alone did NOT fix
  it though - every image anywhere in this repo that has ever rendered
  correctly (broforce's portrait, banksy's picture, this plugin's own
  forecast-table icon) has always been a single lone <img>, never sitting
  directly next to another <img> as a flex sibling. The weather icon is
  now its own single-cell <table> (one <img>, nothing else in the row);
  the clothing icons at the bottom are 1-3 <img> tags side by side in one
  <table> row (each its own <td>) - siblings of EACH OTHER only, never of
  a non-icon element - matching the forecast table's proven "single <img>
  inside a <td>" pattern.

  IMPORTANT: the temperature MUST keep a real TRMNL value--* class (here
  value--xxlarge) rather than a custom inline font-size. TRMNL renders
  "value" numbers through its own pixel/bitmap font system tied to those
  specific classes - an arbitrary font-size outside that set corrupted the
  glyphs AND broke neighboring icons in testing (a whole-row rendering
  artifact, not just a text one). The weather icon itself is no longer
  sized to visually balance the value class in the same row (it's on its
  own row now), so it's simply set to something clearly bigger than
  everything else on the card (144px). The clothing icons at the bottom
  are sized smaller (80px) since there can be up to three side by side.

  current.temperature is itself the average of yr.no + SMHI + Open-Meteo
  (see fetch.mjs) - current.temperature_sources has the individual
  readings if you want to show/debug them.

  Clothing proposal: current.clothing_icon_url is picked from the
  (averaged) current temperature - 8 bands now, from "tank-top" (very hot)
  down through "extreme-cold" (see fetch.mjs's CLOTHING_BANDS); when
  current.needs_rain_gear is true, an umbrella icon is also shown; when
  current.needs_wind_gear is true (wind_speed >= 8 m/s), a windbreaker
  icon is also shown. Up to three icons total, side by side.

  Rain forecast text (centered, below the clothing icons at the bottom):
  current.rain_forecast_text is "Inget regn i sikte!" when no rain is
  expected within the next 60 minutes, or "Det börjar regna kl HH:MM
  idag!" using the local time of the first upcoming yr.no timeseries entry
  (within that window) that indicates rain - see fetch.mjs's
  findRainStart().
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="layout layout--col gap--large" style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">

  <table class="table" style="border: none; width: auto; margin: 0 auto;">
    <tr>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.icon_url }}" width="144" height="144" style="width: 144px; height: 144px;"></td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="layout layout--row" style="justify-content: center;">
    <div class="value value--xxlarge">{{ current.temperature }}°</div>
  </div>

  <div class="layout layout--row" style="justify-content: center;">
    <div class="label">{{ current.condition_text }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="layout layout--row gap--large">
    <div class="item">
      <div class="value value--xlarge">{{ today.high }}° / {{ today.low }}°</div>
      <div class="label">Idag Hög / Låg</div>
    </div>

    <div class="divider divider--vertical"></div>

    <div class="item">
      <div class="value value--large">{{ current.wind_speed }} m/s</div>
      <div class="label">Vind</div>
    </div>

    <div class="item">
      <div class="value value--large">{{ current.humidity }}%</div>
      <div class="label">Luftfuktighet</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <table class="table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Dag</th>
        <th>Väder</th>
        <th>Hög</th>
        <th>Låg</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for day in forecast %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ day.day_name }}</td>
        <td>
          <div class="layout layout--row layout--center-y gap--xsmall">
            <img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ day.icon_url }}" width="26" height="26" style="width: 26px; height: 26px;">
            <span>{{ day.condition_text }}</span>
          </div>
        </td>
        <td>{{ day.high }}°</td>
        <td>{{ day.low }}°</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <table class="table" style="border: none; width: auto; margin: 0 auto;">
    <tr>
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 6px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.clothing_icon_url }}" width="80" height="80" style="width: 80px; height: 80px;"></td>
      {% if current.needs_rain_gear %}
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 6px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.rain_gear_icon_url }}" width="80" height="80" style="width: 80px; height: 80px;"></td>
      {% endif %}
      {% if current.needs_wind_gear %}
      <td style="border: none; padding: 0 6px;"><img class="image image--contain image-dither" src="{{ current.wind_gear_icon_url }}" width="80" height="80" style="width: 80px; height: 80px;"></td>
      {% endif %}
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div class="layout layout--row" style="justify-content: center;">
    <div class="label">{{ current.clothing_text }}</div>
  </div>

  <div class="layout layout--row" style="justify-content: center;">
    <div class="label">{{ current.rain_forecast_text }}</div>
  </div>

</div>

<div class="title_bar" style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;">
  <span class="title">Väder · Alsjön</span>
  <span class="instance">{{ updated_display }}</span>
</div>
